                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 5:\n\nThanks Brad -- changed error() to info() as suggested. Good point about patch splitting too, will keep that in mind for future submissions."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1773079799,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 5:\n\nDeepak: I wrote a mock firmware device (mock_fd) that uses libpldm's pldm_fd_ops callbacks over MCTP serial. It returns CANNOT_BE_UPDATED for one component and CAN_BE_UPDATED for another. Tested on QEMU evb-ast2600 with pldmd over MCTP serial (mctp-serial kernel module + mctpd). I'm planning to clean up mock_fd and submit it to the pldm repo under tools/ so others can reproduce the test. Happy to share details on the setup in the meantime."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1773079808,
            "reviewer": {
