        {
            "timestamp": 1773233731,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 5:\n\nPatch Set 5:\n\nsagar: Brad specifically asked for this to be changed from error() to info() on PS4 \u2014 his reasoning was that COMP_CANNOT_BE_UPDATED is a valid protocol response the BMC is successfully handling, not an error condition. He suggested debug or info level. See Brad's comment on PS4 line 495.\n\nMayank: Good point \u2014 applicableComponents.size() - 1 could underflow if the vector were empty. This code path is unreachable with an empty vector (sendUpdateComponentRequest would never have been called), but I'll add a defensive guard for safety."
        },
        {
