                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "The word Also in a commit message is usually a sign that you should split your patch into multiple.  I might have first done a patch that reverses the order of the return statement and the call to updateDeviceCompletion, then d a patch that calls createRequestFwDataTimer, and then finally a patch that property handles the comp_cannot_be_updated response.  In this case everything is pretty broken and the bugs are all related so its probably ok as is.  Just something to be aware of...reviewers really like to see patches split because it highlights that you respect their time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
